            <ArticleTitle>Isolated spontaneous septal myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>280-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jelectrocard.2011.07.013</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Isolated occlusion of the septal perforating branch of the left anterior descending coronary artery is extremely rare. As a result, little is known about its electrocardiographic manifestations compared with those of an anteroseptal myocardial infarction. We present the case of an isolated septal myocardial infarction with ST-segment elevation.</AbstractText>
